      "id": 1,
      "text": "Cincinnatus takes its name from the Roman general Lucius Quinctius Cincinnatus, a symbol of civic duty.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cincinnatus%2C_New_York",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was carved out of Solon in 1804, becoming one of Cortland County’s original six towns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cincinnatus%2C_New_York",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1984, the Cincinnatus Historic District—14 buildings—earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places.",
